Pre-adapter — runs BEFORE upstream's all_of_them.patch. Reshapes the
haybarn engine source to match the line-by-line context that upstream's
patch expects, so every upstream hunk applies cleanly with zero rejects.

Two engine-vs-upstream divergences need adapting before upstream's
patch can touch them:

1. extension_load.cpp: rebranded error-message string
   "Haybarn extensions are files ending..." → "DuckDB extensions are
   files ending...". Upstream's patch removes this whole line (the
   EndsWith check goes away in wasm builds), so the brand never
   reaches a runtime binary.

2. extension_install_info.hpp: URL constants. The haybarn engine has
   - a long doc-comment explaining the Haybarn R2 layout + http:// reasoning
   - two URL constants pointing at haybarn-extensions.query.farm
   - the upstream nightly repository concept intentionally dropped

   Upstream's patch expects the short upstream-style comment + three
   URL constants (CORE, CORE_NIGHTLY, COMMUNITY) at duckdb.org.
   The pre-adapter rewrites this block to upstream's form so the
   patch's removal context matches. The post-adapter
   (zz-haybarn-engine-restore.patch) restores it after upstream's
   https-flip hunk is done.

When upstream's patch rebases onto a new engine version that
either drops the nightly URL upstream-side, or rewords the error
message context, this adapter can be simplified or deleted.

diff --git a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
--- a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
+++ b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
@@ -454,6 +454,6 @@
 	if (!StringUtil::EndsWith(filename, ".duckdb_extension")) {
 		throw PermissionException(
-		    "Haybarn extensions are files ending with '.duckdb_extension', loading different "
+		    "DuckDB extensions are files ending with '.duckdb_extension', loading different "
 		    "files is not possible, error while loading from '%s', consider 'INSTALL <path>; LOAD <name>;'",
 		    filename);
 	}
